## CHAPTER 11: IMPLEMENTATION ROADMAP

### 11.1 Phase 0 — Foundational Infrastructure (Years 1–3)

**GKG Core Deployment:** Ingest the full PATENTSCOPE corpus (150M+ patents) and top-tier scientific publication databases. Develop and validate the multimodal embedding model. Establish the technical governance protocols for GKG update cadence and completeness auditing.

**MDEP Pilot Program:** Deploy MDEP computation on a sample of 10,000 patent applications per year across 3 volunteer Participating Offices (proposed: USPTO, EPO, JPO — the three offices with the greatest institutional capacity and AI R&D investment). Calibrate index thresholds and validate against human examiner outcomes.

**CSD Framework Consultation:** Conduct multi-stakeholder consultations on the Contribution Stratification Doctrine with industry, civil society, academic legal scholars, and patent office representatives. Draft the disclosure standards for Tiers I–IV.

### 11.2 Phase 1 — Protocol Operationalization (Years 3–7)

**Full MDEP Integration:** MDEP indices become formally advisory in all PO examinations. Examiners receive MDEP briefing sheets for all applications above a filing threshold. Cases with $NI < 0.2$ receive expedited rejection protocols.

**Innovation Commons Launch:** Open the Innovation Commons registration portal, accepting voluntary disclosures from any jurisdiction. Implement the Innovation Credit Score system. Target: 50,000 Commons registrations in the first 3 years.

**Adaptive Protection Term Pilot:** Implement APC-derived term adjustments in the software and algorithm technology classes across POs where national law permits. Monitor welfare outcomes over a 5-year observation period.

### 11.3 Phase 2 — Full Institutional Deployment (Years 7–15)

**Compulsory Licensing Mechanism:** Activate non-use period monitoring and compulsory licensing applications across all participating jurisdictions that have enacted the relevant legislative changes.

**GKG Completeness Expansion:** Expand the corpus to include non-English literature, gray literature, and technical disclosures from developing world institutions. Address the systematic bias toward English-language, high-income-country innovations identified in Phase 0 audits.

**Public Benefit Test Standardization:** Finalize PBT threshold parameters based on Phase 1 empirical data. Implement the market concentration penalty mechanism.

